# Test and development tooling. Compiled to `requirements-dev.txt`; see the header of
# `requirements.in` for the regeneration command and why it must run on Linux.
#
# `-c requirements.txt` constrains this resolution to the versions the runtime lock
# already chose, so the two files can be installed together without pip having to
# reconcile two independent answers.
#
# Nothing here reaches the production image: the Dockerfile installs `requirements.txt`
# only. CI installs both.
-c requirements.txt

